# Maybe Don't CLI Proxy Rules

All CLI commands that interact with external services must be routed through Maybe Don't for validation.

## Required Command Format

```bash
maybe-dont cli -s <server-url> -- <command> [args...]
```

## Rules

1. ALWAYS prefix CLI commands with `maybe-dont cli -s <server-url> --`
2. The `--` separator is REQUIRED between cli flags and the command
3. If a command is denied, explain the denial reason and suggest alternatives
4. Do NOT attempt to bypass validation or run commands directly
5. Use `--dry-run` to validate without executing: `maybe-dont cli -s <url> --dry-run -- <command>`

## Client Identification (Optional)

Set for audit attribution:
```bash
export MAYBE_DONT_CLIENT_ID="your-identifier"
```

## Examples

```bash
# GitHub CLI
maybe-dont cli -s http://localhost:8080 -- gh pr create --title "Feature"

# AWS CLI
maybe-dont cli -s http://localhost:8080 -- aws s3 ls

# Validate without executing
maybe-dont cli -s http://localhost:8080 --dry-run -- rm -rf /tmp/test
```
